Generate an EPAM-branded PowerPoint deck (.pptx, no PDF) summarizing the sFTP usage analysis carried out in this folder on 2026-05-19 against destination DS4_CLH.

Audience: SAP architects + engineering managers, technical-but-not-deep.

Source markdowns (full content lives in `../`, in this analysis arc order):
- ../01-task.md — Goal and task formalization
- ../02-methods.md — Methods discovered (initial pass)
- ../02b-methods-deep.md — Deep dive on candidate methods
- ../02c-code-extracts.md — Relevant code extracts
- ../03-usage-map.md — Where each sFTP entry point is used
- ../04-analysis.md — Cross-cutting findings
- ../05-result.md — Final synthesized result and recommendations
- ../RETRO.md — Retrospective on the run (process, time, costs)

Deck must:
- Open with cover (title, subtitle, date) — EPAM-branded
- Have a contents slide
- One section per analysis phase: Task → Methods → Usage Map → Analysis → Result → Retro
- Use blocks, BlockGrid, and the case-study layout where they fit
- Keep slide bodies short — favor diagrams, blocks, and short bullets over walls of text
- Finish with a thank-you / next-steps slide

Final pptx output: ../report.simple-deck.pptx (NOT overwriting the existing report.pptx).

Generate via the simple-deck Python library; run the resulting `presentation.py` with `simple-deck-python`.
